🧩 LEVEL 1 — BASIC ARRAY PATTERNS
🧠 Pattern 1: Traversal (Basic Looping)

Focus: Looping through arrays, indexing, printing, basic manipulation.
| # | Problem                                              | Platform             | Skill                 |
| - | ---------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------- |
| 1 | Print elements of an array                           | Any (write your own) | Basic for loop        |
| 2 | Find the sum of all elements                         | LeetCode / GFG       | Accumulator logic     |
| 3 | Count even and odd numbers                           | Self                 | If-else + loop        |
| 4 | Count numbers > given value                          | Self                 | Condition inside loop |
| 5 | Find the number of positive, negative, zero elements | GFG                  | Loop & conditions     |
💡 Practice writing loops using both for and while.
🔁 Pattern 2: Reverse Traversal

Focus: Indexing, reverse order, careful boundaries.
| # | Problem                           | Platform                                                                       | Skill                  |
| - | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- |
| 1 | Print array in reverse            | Self                                                                           | Loop from `n-1` to `0` |
| 2 | Reverse array elements (in-place) | LeetCode: [Reverse String #344](https://leetcode.com/problems/reverse-string/) | Two-pointer logic      |
| 3 | Print alternate elements from end | Self                                                                           | Step control in loop   |
💡 Understand indexing: last element = arr[arr.length - 1].

➕ Pattern 3: Sum / Product Pattern
Focus: Aggregation, simple arithmetic with arrays.
| # | Problem                                   | Platform                     | Skill                |
| - | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------- |
| 1 | Sum of elements                           | GFG: “Sum of Array Elements” | Summation            |
| 2 | Average of elements                       | Self                         | Division after sum   |
| 3 | Product of all elements                   | Self                         | Multiplication logic |
| 4 | Find sum of even-indexed elements         | Self                         | Condition on index   |
| 5 | Find difference between even and odd sums | Self                         | Logic building       |
💡 Try to do all in one loop — practice accumulation.
🏆 Pattern 4: Find Min / Max Element
Focus: Comparisons, updating tracking variables.

| # | Problem                                      | Platform       | Skill                         |
| - | -------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------------------- |
| 1 | Find largest element in array                | GFG / LeetCode | `max = Math.max(max, arr[i])` |
| 2 | Find smallest element                        | GFG            | `min = Math.min(min, arr[i])` |
| 3 | Find 2nd largest element                     | GFG            | Sorting or tracking           |
| 4 | Find difference between largest and smallest | Self           | Combine min & max logic       |
| 5 | Check if array is sorted                     | LeetCode Easy  | Adjacent comparisons          |
💡 These are must-know problems — asked in every interview.
🔢 Pattern 5: Counting / Frequency []

